{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>But in the fourth generation they shall come back here</b> — After they go into exile to Egypt, there will be three generations, and so it was: Jacob went into exile; come and count his generations — Judah, Perez, Hezron, and Caleb son of Hezron was among those who entered the Land. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 15:16). And it is not correct at all. And what is correct in my eyes is that \"the fourth generation\" refers to the Amorite who completes his iniquity, for from the day of the decree He prolonged it for him, for He punishes iniquity upon the third generation and upon the fourth, so that if they return, He will not banish them but they will become tribute-bearing servants, or they will clear out before them." "<b>the iniquity of the Amorite</b> — He mentioned the mightiest among them, whose height was like the height of cedars, and they would not be able against him until his measure is filled and his iniquities capture him. And furthermore, it is he who is captured by them, whom they dispossessed at the beginning."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:05.429109106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}